# Vercel deploys this repository with Root Directory = websites/atlas-web, so
# the CLI uploads the repository root and builds from that subdirectory. The
# root is a monorepo containing the desktop app, its packaged build output and
# years of engineering reports: 16,212 files, which exceeds Vercel's 15,000
# file upload limit and makes `vercel deploy` fail outright with
# `missing_archive`.
#
# Nothing excluded here participates in the Next.js build. Keep websites/**
# uploaded; everything below is desktop, packaging, or evidence.

# Committed build output of the desktop app (see the release report: these are
# tracked in git, which is its own cleanup task).
dist
staging
packaging

# Desktop application, its service and its vendored build toolchain.
atlas_desktop
accounts_service
builder_core
licensing
.phase152_packaging_lib
.phase150_inno

# Engineering evidence and benchmark corpora.
reports
benchmarks
external_repos
data
docs
screenshots
website_audit

# Scratch directories left by past test runs.
.phase137a_*
.tmp_phase*
tests_tmp

# Dependencies and build artifacts anywhere in the tree. Vercel installs from
# package-lock.json and builds in its own container.
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/__pycache__

# Local environment files must never be uploaded.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/.env
**/.env.local
